WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.166
How to use AI for product photography with Adobe Firefly

00:00:06.699 --> 00:00:12.131
Step 1 – Open Adobe Firefly
Go to firefly.adobe.com and open the Quick Actions panel.

00:00:13.365 --> 00:00:22.963
Step 2 – Select Generate Background 
Upload your product image from your device or Adobe Cloud Storage.

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:33.427
Step 3 – Ensure a Clean Source Image  
Use a high‑resolution product photo for best results.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:40.026
Step 4 – Remove Background if Needed  
Use the Remove Background tool to isolate the product.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:50.224
Step 5 – Adjust Prompt Settings  
Choose your AI model, output size, and image quality.

00:00:50.357 --> 00:00:56.080
Step 6 – Write a Strong Prompt  

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:02.122
Describe lighting, mood, composition, and photography style — not just objects.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.021
Step 7 – Generate Your First Scene  
Click Generate and review the results.

00:01:08.021 --> 00:01:13.686
Step 8 – Refine the Prompt  
Small adjustments can dramatically improve realism and style.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:23.184
Step 9 – Add Branding Details  
Generate again with prompts describing label placement or typography.

00:01:24.351 --> 00:01:33.182
Step 10 – Create Multiple Formats  
Use Expand to resize the canvas for social posts, ads, or banners.

00:01:33.349 --> 00:01:43.680
Step 11 – Build a Full Campaign  
Generate variations with different angles, crops, and compositions.

00:01:44.014 --> 00:01:54.012
Step 12 – Keep Visuals Consistent  
Match lighting, color palette, and props across all images.

